WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.349
The next exam topic is actually in the form of a question: why use IP version 4? The answer is simple. It has been the standard for IP addresses for decades.

00:10.349 --> 00:19.911
And, it is easy to use and configure. For example, you can plug most devices into a network and automatically obtain an IPv4 address.

00:19.911 --> 00:30.755
It will probably be a private address, but that will allow you to connect to other devices on a network. The other reason: IPv6 is not yet universally implemented.

00:30.755 --> 00:44.610
Even though the IPv4 address space is running out, or has run out, technically, we are years, possibly decades away from IPv6 becoming the de facto standard for all networks.

